  "slug": "cross-power-spectrum-b133",
  "summary": "Four preprints extend simulation validation: a Lyman-alpha emulator, w(z) mapping onto constant-w runs, and wave-phase resolution criteria for scalar-field dark matter.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is extending the reach of expensive simulations through field-level mappings validated against reference runs. One paper trains a 3D U-Net to map density and velocity fields to Lyman-alpha flux, reproducing P1D, bispectrum and trispectrum across IllustrisTNG and FLAMINGO. Two papers show that N-body dynamics depend on the expansion history a(τ), so constant-w simulations can reproduce CPL and general w(z) models, with power spectra agreeing within 0.2% in one case. A fourth builds matched LCDM-SFDM initial conditions linking CLASS-SFDM, MUSIC and AxioNyx, and finds that accurate density recovery does not guarantee adequate wave-phase resolution. New relative to the prior synthesis is the dark-matter initial-condition validation; the CAMELS gas emulator and DESI-BGS assembly-bias test are not in the current items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
